## Layout: Horizontal extension (forms, cards, copy)

- **Horizontal extension, not vertical**: Forms, cards, and text must use the full content width. Never squeeze UI into a tall narrow strip with one word per line.
- **Width utilities (Tailwind v4 + this repo)**:
  - **Safe**: `w-full`, `min-w-0`, `max-w-6xl`, `max-w-7xl`, `max-w-[min(100%,48rem)]`, or explicit `max-w-[…rem]`.
  - **Unsafe — do not use on forms/cards/containers**: `max-w-xs`, `max-w-sm`, `max-w-md`, `max-w-lg`, `max-w-xl`, `max-w-2xl`, `max-w-3xl`, `max-w-4xl`, `max-w-5xl` unless you verify computed width in DevTools (they were broken when `--spacing-*` lived in `@theme`).
  - **Never** add `--spacing-xs` … `--spacing-3xl` to the `@theme { }` block in `globals.css` — they override `max-w-*` and cause ~24px–64px-wide layouts.
- **Forms (mobile-first)**: `w-full min-w-[280px] max-w-6xl`; field grids `grid-cols-2` on mobile where possible; inputs `w-full min-w-0`.
- **Avoid**: CSS `columns`, flex children without `min-w-0` in shrink contexts, `max-w-*` without checking rendered width.
- **Modals and cards**: `min-w-[280px]`, `w-full`, `shrink-0` inside flex parents when needed.

